IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- what an employee (and a platform worker) meets.
--
-- SEAT: the employee -- or, for a delivery rider on a digital labour platform, the regulated worker (the employee-like
-- worker of s 15P). "What must my employer give me and pay me, and what can I claim?" Every question below is phrased as
-- that person would ask it, on facts that person could state.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Who is an employee (s 12 "vocational placement", "junior employee"; s 13; s 15AA as an input);
-- the employee-like worker (ss 15N, 15P), what a minimum standards order may say (ss 536KL, 536KM, 536KMA) and
-- protection from unfair deactivation (ss 536LD, 536LU, with s 15C); service when changing employer (s 22(5), (7));
-- small business employer (s 23); the National Employment Standards the lives turn on -- flexible working requests
-- (ss 65, 65A), unpaid parental leave (ss 67, 70, 71, 72A, 76, 84), annual leave (ss 87, 90), personal/carer's leave
-- (s 96), compassionate leave (s 104), family and domestic violence leave (s 106A), jury service (s 111), public
-- holidays (ss 114-116), superannuation (s 116B), notice of termination (ss 117, 118), redundancy pay (ss 119, 121,
-- 123); modern awards (s 45); unfair dismissal (ss 382, 383, 385, 386, 389, 392, 394); notice to Centrelink (s 530);
-- pay slips (s 536); recovering an underpayment (ss 544, 545, 548).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73, compilation date 7 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 62, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00355), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt.
-- Regulations used: Fair Work Regulations 2009 (F2009L02356), Compilation No. 57, compilation date 1 October 2026
-- (register id F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../../fair-work-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt
-- -- regs 1.08AA (contractor high income threshold), 2.00 (flexible unpaid parental leave days), 2.13 (high income
-- threshold indexation), 3.46 (pay slip contents), 4.01 (choosing the small claims procedure).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The modern awards themselves (General Retail, Security Services, Cleaning Services: junior rates,
-- overtime, shift penalties and minimum rates are INPUTS) and the national minimum wage order (an INPUT) -- none is
-- deposited; the current high income threshold and contractor high income threshold figures (INPUTS, with the floors
-- the Regulations guarantee); the s 15AA multi-factor test (an INPUT) and the s 15AB opt-out; enterprise agreements;
-- the s 87(3) shiftworker test; long service leave (s 113 turns on pre-2010 award terms and State law); casual
-- conversion (Division 4A); s 120 (FWC reduces redundancy pay), s 121(4) (insolvent small business), s 122 (transfer
-- and redundancy pay); the general protections (Part 3-1); civil penalty amounts; the employer's side of every duty
-- beyond what it means for the employee; the FWC, the Ombudsman and the courts as institutions (machinery).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- the employee's questions`

§§ `ss 12, 13, 15AA -- am I an employee`

-- s 13: "A national system employee is an individual so far as he or she is employed, or usually employed ... by a
-- national system employer, except on a vocational placement."
-- s 12: "vocational placement means a placement that is: (a) undertaken with an employer for which a person is not
-- entitled to be paid any remuneration; and (b) undertaken as a requirement of an education or training course; and
-- (c) authorised under a law or an administrative arrangement of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory."
-- s 15AA: "employee" in its ordinary meaning turns on "the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the
-- relationship" -- a multi-factor judgment, asked here as a fact.
@export Am I on a vocational placement (s 12), and so outside the Act's minimum standards?
GIVEN `I am entitled to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to be paid anything for the placement
      `my course requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the placement is a requirement of your education or training course
      `a law or government arrangement authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Commonwealth, State or Territory law or administrative arrangement authorises the placement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I on a vocational placement` IF
        (NOT `I am entitled to be paid`)
    AND `my course requires it`
    AND `a law or government arrangement authorises it`

@export Am I a national system employee (s 13)?
GIVEN `I am an employee in the ordinary meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, looking at the real substance of the relationship (s 15AA), you are an employee rather than a contractor
      `my employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a national system employer (for example, a company)
      `I am on a vocational placement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on an unpaid vocational placement (s 12)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a national system employee` IF
        `I am an employee in the ordinary meaning`
    AND `my employer is a national system employer`
    AND (NOT `I am on a vocational placement`)

-- s 12: "junior employee means a national system employee who is under 21." The junior RATE is in the modern award
-- (s 139(1)(a)), not deposited: an input.
@export Am I a junior employee (s 12), to whom an award's junior rates can apply?
GIVEN `how old I am` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a junior employee` IF
    `how old I am` LESS THAN 21

§§ `ss 15N, 15P, 536KL-536KMA -- am I an employee-like worker, and what can an order give me`

-- s 15P(1): an employee-like worker (a) is an individual party to a services contract who performs work under it; (b)
-- "performs all, or a significant majority, of the work"; (c) the work is "digital platform work" (s 15N: work by an
-- independent contractor "through or by means of a digital labour platform" for which "payment is made"); (d) "does
-- not perform any work under the services contract as an employee"; and (e) "satisfies 2 or more of" (i) "low
-- bargaining power", (ii) "remuneration at or below the rate of an employee performing comparable work", (iii) "a low
-- degree of authority over the performance of the work", (iv) prescribed characteristics.
DECLARE PlatformWork HAS
    `I am an individual party to the services contract and do the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I do all or a significant majority of the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is paid and done through a digital labour platform` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I do some of the work as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have low bargaining power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am paid at or below a comparable employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have little authority over how I do the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a prescribed characteristic` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if` MEANS IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

@export Am I an employee-like worker (s 15P)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A PlatformWork @desc The facts of your platform work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an employee-like worker` IF
        `my work`'s `I am an individual party to the services contract and do the work`
    AND `my work`'s `I do all or a significant majority of the work`
    AND `my work`'s `the work is paid and done through a digital labour platform`
    AND (NOT `my work`'s `I do some of the work as an employee`)
    AND     `one if` (`my work`'s `I have low bargaining power`)
          PLUS `one if` (`my work`'s `I am paid at or below a comparable employee`)
          PLUS `one if` (`my work`'s `I have little authority over how I do the work`)
          PLUS `one if` (`my work`'s `I have a prescribed characteristic`)
        AT LEAST 2

-- s 536KL(1): an order "may include terms about" (a) payment terms; (b) deductions; (d) record-keeping; (e) insurance;
-- (f) consultation; (g) representation; (h) delegates' rights; (i) cost recovery (no paragraph (c) in the deposit);
-- (2) the list does "not limit the terms that may be included". s 536KM(1): "must not include terms about" (a)
-- "overtime rates"; (b) "rostering arrangements"; (d) "a term that deems a regulated worker to be an employee".
-- s 536KMA(1): an employee-like worker order must not include (a) "penalty rates", (c) "minimum periods of engagement";
-- but (2) may "if the FWC is satisfied that the inclusion of the term is appropriate". READING (an inference):
-- superannuation is neither listed nor barred, and the list is non-limiting, so the Act does not exclude it.
DECLARE OrderTerm IS ONE OF
    `payment terms`
    `deductions`
    `insurance`
    `superannuation`
    `overtime rates`
    `rostering arrangements`
    `a term deeming me an employee`
    `penalty rates`
    `minimum periods of engagement`

@export Can a minimum standards order for employee-like workers give me this term (ss 536KL, 536KM, 536KMA)?
GIVEN `the term` IS AN OrderTerm @desc The kind of term you want the order to contain
      `if the FWC is satisfied the term is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For penalty rates or minimum engagement: whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied the term is appropriate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an order give me this term` IF
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `overtime rates` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `rostering arrangements` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a term deeming me an employee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `penalty rates` THEN `if the FWC is satisfied the term is appropriate`
    WHEN `minimum periods of engagement` THEN `if the FWC is satisfied the term is appropriate`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 15C, 536LD, 536LU and reg 1.08AA -- am I protected from unfair deactivation`

-- s 536LD: protected if "(a) the person is an employee-like worker", (b) works through a digital labour platform, and
-- (c) has been doing so "on a regular basis for a period of at least 6 months". s 536LU(2): no application unless the
-- annual rate of earnings "is less than the contractor high income threshold"; (3) "within 21 days after the
-- deactivation". Reg 1.08AA(2): the threshold for 2024-25 "is $175,000"; (3) later years are indexed, and a rounded
-- ratio "less than 1 ... becomes 1"; s 15C(2): a regulation cannot reduce it. So the threshold is never below $175,000:
-- a figure entered below that floor is lifted to it.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contractor high income threshold is never below` MEANS 175000

@export Can I apply to the FWC about an unfair deactivation from a platform (ss 536LD, 536LU)?
GIVEN `I am an employee-like worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee-like worker (s 15P)
      `months I have worked regularly on the platform` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you have worked on the platform on a regular basis
      `my annual earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual rate of earnings, in dollars
      `the contractor high income threshold this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The contractor high income threshold for the year (reg 1.08AA), or 0 if you do not know it
      `days since the deactivation took effect` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the deactivation took effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply about an unfair deactivation` IF
        `I am an employee-like worker`
    AND `months I have worked regularly on the platform` AT LEAST 6
    AND `my annual earnings` LESS THAN max `the contractor high income threshold this year` `the contractor high income threshold is never below`
    AND `days since the deactivation took effect` AT MOST 21

§§ `ss 22(5), 22(7), 23 -- service, changing employer, small business`

-- s 22(5): on a "transfer of employment", "any period of service of the employee with the first employer counts as
-- service of the employee with the second employer". s 22(7)(a): a transfer where the employee "becomes employed by the
-- second employer not more than 3 months after the termination" and the employers "are associated entities"; (b) a
-- transferring employee in a transfer of business. Otherwise service with a new employer starts from nothing.
@export Does my service with my old employer count with my new one (s 22(5))?
GIVEN `months between the two jobs` IS A NUMBER @desc Months between leaving the old employer and starting with the new one
      `the employers are associated entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the two employers are associated entities (for example, companies in the same group)
      `I moved with a transfer of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you moved as part of a transfer of the business to the new employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my old service count` IF
        (`months between the two jobs` AT MOST 3 AND `the employers are associated entities`)
    OR  `I moved with a transfer of business`

-- s 23(1): a small business employer "employs fewer than 15 employees"; (2)(b) casuals counted only if regular; (4)
-- the count includes the employee being dismissed and others also being dismissed.
GIVEN `employees counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my employer is a small business employer` IF
    `employees counted` LESS THAN 15

§§ `ss 65, 65A -- may I ask for flexible work, and when may it be refused`

-- s 65(1A): circumstances include "(aa) the employee is pregnant; (a) the employee is the parent, or has responsibility
-- for the care, of a child who is of school age or younger"; carer, disability, 55 or older, family and domestic
-- violence. (1B) a parent "returning to work after taking leave in relation to the birth" "may request to work
-- part-time". (2) "(a) for an employee other than a casual employee -- ... at least 12 months of continuous service ...
-- immediately before making the request; or (b) for a casual employee -- ... a regular casual employee ... for ... at
-- least 12 months; and ... a reasonable expectation of continuing employment". (3) "in writing", with "details of the
-- change sought and of the reasons". s 22(4): for this Division unpaid parental leave counts toward the 12 months.
@export May I make a flexible working request (s 65)?
GIVEN `a listed circumstance applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are pregnant, a parent of a child of school age or younger, a carer, have a disability, are 55 or older, or are affected by family and domestic violence
      `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `months of continuous service` IS A NUMBER @desc Months of continuous service with this employer immediately before the request
      `I am a regular casual of 12 months expecting to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a casual: whether you have been a regular casual for at least 12 months and reasonably expect to continue
      `my request is in writing with details and reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your request is in writing and says what you want changed and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a flexible working request` IF
        `a listed circumstance applies to me`
    AND `my request is in writing with details and reasons`
    AND (    ((NOT `I am casual`) AND `months of continuous service` AT LEAST 12)
         OR  (`I am casual` AND `I am a regular casual of 12 months expecting to continue`))

-- s 65A(1): "a written response to the request within 21 days". (3): "may refuse the request only if: (a) the employer
-- has: (i) discussed the request with the employee; and (ii) genuinely tried to reach an agreement ...; and (b) ... have
-- not reached such an agreement; and (c) the employer has had regard to the consequences of the refusal for the
-- employee; and (d) the refusal is on reasonable business grounds".
@export Within how many days must my employer answer my flexible working request in writing (s 65A(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days does my employer have to answer` IS 21

@export May my employer refuse my flexible working request (s 65A(3))?
GIVEN `it discussed the request with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer discussed the request with you
      `it genuinely tried to reach agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer genuinely tried to reach an agreement with you
      `we reached agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer agreed on a change
      `it considered the consequences for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer had regard to the consequences of refusal for you
      `if it has reasonable business grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal is on reasonable business grounds (for example, too costly, or a significant loss of productivity)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer refuse my request` IF
        `it discussed the request with me`
    AND `it genuinely tried to reach agreement`
    AND (NOT `we reached agreement`)
    AND `it considered the consequences for me`
    AND `if it has reasonable business grounds`

§§ `ss 67, 70, 71, 72A, 76, 84 and reg 2.00 -- unpaid parental leave`

-- s 70: "12 months of unpaid parental leave" if the leave is associated with the birth (or adoption placement) of a
-- child and the employee "has or will have a responsibility for the care of the child".
-- s 67(1): a non-casual is not entitled "unless the employee has, or will have, completed at least 12 months of
-- continuous service with the employer immediately before the date that applies under subsection (3)"; (3) that date is
-- "the expected date of birth of the child" for "birth-related leave starting before the birth", otherwise "the date on
-- which the employee's period of leave is to start". (2): a casual must be a regular casual for at least 12 months who
-- would reasonably expect to continue.
@export Am I entitled to 12 months of unpaid parental leave (ss 67, 70)?
GIVEN `I will care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have or will have responsibility for the care of the child
      `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `I am a regular casual of 12 months expecting to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a casual: whether you have been a regular casual for at least 12 months and would reasonably expect to continue
      `the day I started with this employer` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer began
      `the expected date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's expected date of birth
      `the day my leave starts` IS A DATE @desc The day your leave is to start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to unpaid parental leave` IF
        `I will care for the child`
    AND (    ((NOT `I am casual`) AND `add months` `the day I started with this employer` 12 AT MOST `the date that applies`)
         OR  (`I am casual` AND `I am a regular casual of 12 months expecting to continue`))
    WHERE
        `the date that applies` MEANS
            IF `the day my leave starts` LESS THAN `the expected date of birth`
            THEN `the expected date of birth`
            ELSE `the day my leave starts`

-- s 71(3): a pregnant employee's birth-related leave "may start: (a) up to 6 weeks before the expected date of birth of
-- the child; or (b) earlier, if the employer and employee so agree".
@export May my parental leave start this many weeks before the expected birth (s 71(3))?
GIVEN `weeks before the expected birth` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks before the expected date of birth you want the leave to start
      `my employer agrees to an earlier start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer agrees to an earlier start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my leave start that early` IF
        `weeks before the expected birth` AT MOST 6
    OR  `my employer agrees to an earlier start`

-- s 72A(1): "up to 100 days (or, if a higher number of days is prescribed by the regulations, that higher number of
-- days)" of flexible unpaid parental leave in the 24 months from the birth; it "comes out of" the 12 months (Note 1).
-- Reg 2.00: if the date of birth is from 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025, 110 days; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026, 120
-- days; "on or after 1 July 2026 -- 130 days".
@export How many days of flexible unpaid parental leave may I take (s 72A, reg 2.00)?
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth (or day of placement for adoption)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many flexible days may I take` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date of birth` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2026 THEN 130
        IF `the date of birth` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2025 THEN 120
        IF `the date of birth` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2024 THEN 110
        OTHERWISE 100

-- s 76(1): an extension "for a further period of up to 12 months" may be requested; (7) not "beyond 24 months after the
-- date of birth".
@export At most how many months of unpaid parental leave can I have, with an extension (ss 70, 76)?
GIVEN `months of extension I request` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of extension beyond the first 12 you request
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months of leave at most` IS
    min (12 PLUS min `months of extension I request` 12) 24

-- The Act once limited concurrent leave by both parents (former s 72); the deposit has no s 72 in Part 2-2, and the
-- transitional note (Schedule 2 to the amending Act) treats old "concurrent leave" as flexible unpaid parental leave.
-- READING: nothing in the deposited Act stops an entitled employee taking leave while the other parent is on leave.
@export May I take my unpaid parental leave at the same time as the other parent?
GIVEN `I am entitled to unpaid parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to unpaid parental leave (ss 67, 70)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take leave at the same time as the other parent` IF
    `I am entitled to unpaid parental leave`

-- s 84: "On ending a period of unpaid parental leave, an employee is entitled to return to: (a) the employee's
-- pre-parental leave position; or (b) if that position no longer exists -- an available position for which the
-- employee is qualified and suited nearest in status and pay".
@export What job am I entitled to come back to after parental leave (s 84)?
GIVEN `my old position still exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your pre-parental leave position still exists
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What job do I come back to` IS
    IF `my old position still exists`
    THEN "my pre-parental leave position"
    ELSE "an available position I am qualified and suited for, nearest in status and pay"

§§ `ss 87, 90, 96, 104, 106A -- leave`

-- s 87(1): "For each year of service ... (other than periods of employment as a casual employee ...), an employee is
-- entitled to: (a) 4 weeks of paid annual leave; or (b) 5 weeks" for a shiftworker. (2) it "accrues progressively ...
-- according to the employee's ordinary hours of work". s 96(1): "10 days of paid personal/carer's leave", casuals
-- excluded; (2) accrues the same way. READING: the accrued amounts assume the same ordinary hours every month.
@export How many weeks of paid annual leave do I get each year (s 87)?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `an award or agreement makes me a shiftworker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a modern award or enterprise agreement defines you as a shiftworker
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of annual leave a year` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am casual` THEN 0
        IF `an award or agreement makes me a shiftworker` THEN 5
        OTHERWISE 4

@export How many days of paid personal/carer's leave do I get each year (s 96)?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of personal leave a year` IS
    IF `I am casual` THEN 0 ELSE 10

@export How many weeks of annual leave have I accrued (s 87(2))?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `an award or agreement makes me a shiftworker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a modern award or enterprise agreement defines you as a shiftworker
      `months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc Months of service so far
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of annual leave accrued` IS
    `How many weeks of annual leave a year` `I am casual` `an award or agreement makes me a shiftworker` TIMES `months of service` DIVIDED BY 12

@export How many days of personal/carer's leave have I accrued (s 96(2))?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `months of service` IS A NUMBER @desc Months of service so far
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of personal leave accrued` IS
    `How many days of personal leave a year` `I am casual` TIMES `months of service` DIVIDED BY 12

-- s 90(2): "If, when the employment of an employee ends, the employee has a period of untaken paid annual leave, the
-- employer must pay the employee the amount that would have been payable ... had the employee taken that period of
-- leave"; (1) at the "base rate of pay for the employee's ordinary hours of work". However the employment ends.
@export How much must I be paid for untaken annual leave when my job ends (s 90(2))?
GIVEN `untaken ordinary hours of annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of annual leave you have not taken
      `my base hourly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your base rate of pay per hour, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much for untaken annual leave` IS
    `untaken ordinary hours of annual leave` TIMES `my base hourly rate`

-- s 104(1): "2 days of compassionate leave for each occasion" (life-threatening illness or injury, or death, of a member
-- of the immediate family or household; stillbirth; miscarriage). s 106: paid for non-casuals; "For casual employees,
-- compassionate leave is unpaid leave."
@export How many days of compassionate leave do I get for each occasion, and is it paid (ss 104, 106)?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many paid days of compassionate leave per occasion` IS
    IF `I am casual` THEN 0 ELSE 2

-- s 106A(1): "10 days of paid family and domestic violence leave in a 12 month period"; (2)(c) "available in full to
-- part-time and casual employees".
@export How many days of paid family and domestic violence leave do I get in a 12-month period (s 106A)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of family and domestic violence leave` IS 10

§§ `s 111 -- jury service`

-- s 111(1): applies to an employee absent "because of jury service" who "is not a casual employee". (2) pay "at the
-- employee's base rate of pay for the employee's ordinary hours of work". (4) if evidence is required, no payment
-- "unless the employee provides the evidence", and the payment "is reduced by the total amount of jury service pay".
-- (5) "only required to pay the employee for the first 10 days of absence". Jury service pay is set by State law: an
-- INPUT. READING: the Act is silent if jury pay exceeds base pay; the payment does not go below nil.
@export How much must my employer pay me while I am on jury service (s 111)?
GIVEN `I am casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a casual employee
      `days I am absent` IS A NUMBER @desc Days absent for this jury summons
      `my base pay per day` IS A NUMBER @desc Your base pay for a day of ordinary hours, in dollars
      `jury service pay for the first 10 days` IS A NUMBER @desc Jury service pay you get under State law for the first 10 days, in dollars
      `my employer asks for evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer requires evidence of your jury service pay
      `I give the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give that evidence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much jury service pay from my employer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am casual` THEN 0
        IF `my employer asks for evidence` AND (NOT `I give the evidence`) THEN 0
        IF `my employer asks for evidence`
            THEN max (min `days I am absent` 10 TIMES `my base pay per day` MINUS `jury service pay for the first 10 days`) 0
        OTHERWISE min `days I am absent` 10 TIMES `my base pay per day`

§§ `ss 114-116 -- public holidays`

-- s 115(1)(a): New Year's Day, Australia Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, Anzac Day, the Sovereign's birthday holiday
-- (as celebrated in the State), Christmas Day, Boxing Day; (b) "any other day ... declared or prescribed by or under a
-- law of a State or Territory to be observed generally ... as a public holiday". Whether the WA law declares a day is an
-- input. s 116: absent on a public holiday, paid "at the employee's base rate of pay for the employee's ordinary hours
-- of work on the day".
DECLARE Holiday IS ONE OF
    `New Year's Day`
    `Australia Day`
    `Good Friday`
    `Easter Monday`
    `Anzac Day`
    `the Sovereign's birthday holiday`
    `Christmas Day`
    `Boxing Day`
    `Western Australia Day`
    `Labour Day`
    `Melbourne Cup Day`

@export Is this day a public holiday for me (s 115)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A Holiday @desc The day
      `if my State's law declares it a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a day not named in s 115(1)(a): whether your State or Territory's law declares it a public holiday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a public holiday for me` IF
    CONSIDER `the day`
    WHEN `Western Australia Day` THEN `if my State's law declares it a public holiday`
    WHEN `Labour Day` THEN `if my State's law declares it a public holiday`
    WHEN `Melbourne Cup Day` THEN `if my State's law declares it a public holiday`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 116B -- superannuation`

-- s 116B: "An employer must make contributions to a superannuation fund for the benefit of an employee so as to avoid
-- liability to pay superannuation guarantee charge". Whether the charge would arise (age, hours, the percentage) is a
-- question of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992: an input here.
@export Must my employer pay superannuation for me under the National Employment Standards (s 116B)?
GIVEN `if the super guarantee charge would otherwise apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992, your employer would owe the super guarantee charge for you without contributions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer pay my super` IF
    `if the super guarantee charge would otherwise apply to me`

§§ `ss 117-123 -- notice and redundancy pay`

-- s 117(1)-(2): "An employer must not terminate an employee's employment unless" it gives written notice of at least
-- the minimum period, or payment in lieu. (3) on "continuous service with the employer at the end of the day the
-- notice is given": "Not more than 1 year -- 1 week"; "More than 1 year but not more than 3 years -- 2 weeks"; "More
-- than 3 years but not more than 5 years -- 3 weeks"; "More than 5 years -- 4 weeks"; "(b) then increase the period by
-- 1 week if the employee is over 45 years old and has completed at least 2 years of continuous service". (4) casual
-- service does not count. s 118: an award or agreement "may include terms specifying the period of notice an employee
-- must give" -- the Act sets none for a resignation. s 123(1): the Division does not apply to "(a) an employee employed
-- for a specified period of time, for a specified task, or for the duration of a specified season; (b) an employee
-- whose employment is terminated because of serious misconduct; (c) a casual employee".
-- READING (an inference): "over 45 years old" means older than 45, so 45 exactly does not qualify.
DECLARE HowItEnded IS ONE OF
    `my employer ended it`
    `I resigned`

DECLARE MyTermination HAS
    `how it ended` IS A HowItEnded
    `I was casual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was employed for a specified period, task or season` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was for serious misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years of continuous service` IS A NUMBER
    `my age` IS A NUMBER
    `my job is no longer needed by anyone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer is insolvent or bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employees counted under s 23` IS A NUMBER
    `I am an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an industry-specific redundancy scheme in my award applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `t` IS A MyTermination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 11 covers me` IF
        (NOT `t`'s `I was casual`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `I was employed for a specified period, task or season`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `it was for serious misconduct`)

GIVEN `t` IS A MyTermination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ended by my employer` IF
    CONSIDER `t`'s `how it ended`
    WHEN `my employer ended it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 117(3) table in weeks` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `years` AT MOST 1 THEN 1
        IF `years` AT MOST 3 THEN 2
        IF `years` AT MOST 5 THEN 3
        OTHERWISE 4

@export How many weeks' notice (or pay in lieu) must my employer give me (s 117)?
GIVEN `t` IS A MyTermination @desc How your employment ended
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of notice must I get` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`ended by my employer` `t` AND `Division 11 covers me` `t`) THEN 0
        IF `t`'s `my age` GREATER THAN 45 AND `t`'s `years of continuous service` AT LEAST 2
            THEN `the s 117(3) table in weeks` (`t`'s `years of continuous service`) PLUS 1
        OTHERWISE `the s 117(3) table in weeks` (`t`'s `years of continuous service`)

-- s 119(1): redundancy pay if employment is terminated "(a) at the employer's initiative because the employer no
-- longer requires the job done by the employee to be done by anyone, except where this is due to the ordinary and
-- customary turnover of labour; or (b) because of the insolvency or bankruptcy of the employer." (2) table on
-- continuous service "on termination": at least 1 but less than 2 years -- 4 weeks; 2-3 -- 6; 3-4 -- 7; 4-5 -- 8; 5-6
-- -- 10; 6-7 -- 11; 7-8 -- 13; 8-9 -- 14; 9-10 -- 16; "At least 10 years -- 12 weeks". s 121(1): not if "(a) ...
-- continuous service ... is less than 12 months; or (b) the employer is a small business employer". s 123(4): not for
-- "(a) an employee who is an apprentice; or (b) an employee to whom an industry-specific redundancy scheme in a modern
-- award applies". s 22(2)(b): unpaid leave does not count as service here; years are taken as already net of it.
-- READING (an inference): termination "because of the insolvency" is read as a termination by the employer.
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 119(2) table in weeks` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `years` LESS THAN 1  THEN 0
        IF `years` LESS THAN 2  THEN 4
        IF `years` LESS THAN 3  THEN 6
        IF `years` LESS THAN 4  THEN 7
        IF `years` LESS THAN 5  THEN 8
        IF `years` LESS THAN 6  THEN 10
        IF `years` LESS THAN 7  THEN 11
        IF `years` LESS THAN 8  THEN 13
        IF `years` LESS THAN 9  THEN 14
        IF `years` LESS THAN 10 THEN 16
        OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `t` IS A MyTermination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am entitled to redundancy pay` IF
        `Division 11 covers me` `t`
    AND `ended by my employer` `t`
    AND (    (`t`'s `my job is no longer needed by anyone` AND (NOT `t`'s `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour`))
         OR  `t`'s `my employer is insolvent or bankrupt`)
    AND `t`'s `years of continuous service` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT (`my employer is a small business employer` (`t`'s `employees counted under s 23`)))
    AND (NOT `t`'s `I am an apprentice`)
    AND (NOT `t`'s `an industry-specific redundancy scheme in my award applies`)

@export How many weeks of redundancy pay do I get (ss 119, 121, 123)?
GIVEN `t` IS A MyTermination @desc How your employment ended
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of redundancy pay do I get` IS
    IF `I am entitled to redundancy pay` `t`
    THEN `the s 119(2) table in weeks` (`t`'s `years of continuous service`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 45 -- modern awards`

-- s 45: "A person must not contravene a term of a modern award." s 46(1): only if the award "applies". The award's
-- rates (junior rates, overtime, cleaning minimums) are not deposited: inputs.
@export Has my employer contravened my modern award (s 45)?
GIVEN `the award applies to my employer and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the modern award applies to your employer and you
      `a term of the award was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer did not comply with a term (for example, paid overtime at ordinary time where the award sets a higher rate)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer contravened my award` IF
        `the award applies to my employer and me`
    AND `a term of the award was not complied with`

§§ `ss 382-394, reg 2.13 -- unfair dismissal`

-- s 383: "(a) if the employer is not a small business employer -- 6 months ...; (b) if the employer is a small business
-- employer -- one year". s 382: protected if the person "has completed a period of employment ... of at least the
-- minimum employment period" and (i) "a modern award covers the person", (ii) an enterprise agreement applies, or (iii)
-- annual earnings are "less than the high income threshold". Reg 2.13: the threshold started from "$100 000" indexed,
-- and each year's rounded ratio "less than 1 ... becomes 1", so it never falls below $100,000. A figure entered below
-- that floor is lifted to it. The Act says nothing of "probation".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the high income threshold is never below` MEANS 100000

@export How many months must I work before I am protected from unfair dismissal (s 383)?
GIVEN `employees counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees your employer has (casuals only if regular, and counting anyone being dismissed with you)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months before I am protected` IS
    IF `my employer is a small business employer` `employees counted` THEN 12 ELSE 6

@export Am I protected from unfair dismissal (s 382)?
GIVEN `months I have been employed` IS A NUMBER @desc Months of continuous service with this employer
      `employees counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees your employer has
      `a modern award covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a modern award covers you
      `an enterprise agreement applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enterprise agreement applies to you
      `my annual earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual rate of earnings, in dollars
      `the high income threshold this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold for the year (reg 2.13), or 0 if you do not know it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from unfair dismissal` IF
        `months I have been employed` AT LEAST `How many months before I am protected` `employees counted`
    AND (    `a modern award covers me`
         OR  `an enterprise agreement applies to me`
         OR  `my annual earnings` LESS THAN max `the high income threshold this year` `the high income threshold is never below`)

-- Reg 2.13(3): next year's threshold is last year's times the AWOTE ratio, "Round the result to 3 decimal places. If
-- the fourth decimal place is 5 or above, round it up. If the rounded result is less than 1, the rounded result becomes
-- 1"; then "round the result to the nearest multiple of $100. If the result is a multiple of $50, round it up".
@export What is this year's high income threshold, from last year's and the earnings index (reg 2.13(3))?
GIVEN `last year's threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold for the previous year, in dollars
      `AWOTE in effect this 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc Average weekly ordinary time earnings in effect on 1 July this year
      `AWOTE in effect last 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc Average weekly ordinary time earnings in effect on 1 July last year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is this year's high income threshold` IS
    TRUNC (`last year's threshold` TIMES `the ratio` DIVIDED BY 100 PLUS 0.5) 0 TIMES 100
    WHERE
        `the ratio` MEANS
            max (TRUNC (`AWOTE in effect this 1 July` DIVIDED BY `AWOTE in effect last 1 July` TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5) 0 DIVIDED BY 1000) 1

-- s 386(1): "dismissed" if "(a) ... terminated on the employer's initiative; or (b) ... resigned ... but was forced to
-- do so because of conduct ... engaged in by his or her employer"; (2)(a) not when a specified-period, task or season
-- contract ends. s 385: unfairly dismissed "if the FWC is satisfied that" (a) dismissed; (b) "harsh, unjust or
-- unreasonable"; (c) "not consistent with the Small Business Fair Dismissal Code"; (d) "not a case of genuine
-- redundancy". s 389(1): genuine redundancy if the job is no longer required "because of changes in the operational
-- requirements" and the employer "has complied with any obligation in a modern award or enterprise agreement ... to
-- consult"; (2) not if "it would have been reasonable in all the circumstances for the person to be redeployed".
@export Was my dismissal a case of genuine redundancy (s 389)?
GIVEN `my job is no longer needed because of operational changes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer no longer needs anyone to do your job because of changes in its operational requirements
      `my employer consulted as the award or agreement required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer met any duty in the award or agreement to consult about the redundancy
      `if redeploying me would have been reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it would have been reasonable to redeploy you in the business or an associated entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it a genuine redundancy` IF
        `my job is no longer needed because of operational changes`
    AND `my employer consulted as the award or agreement required`
    AND (NOT `if redeploying me would have been reasonable`)

@export Was I unfairly dismissed (ss 385, 386)?
GIVEN `my employer ended my job, or forced me to resign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer ended your employment, or you resigned because your employer's conduct forced you to
      `only a fixed term, task or season ran out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment simply ended at the end of a specified period, task or season
      `if the FWC is satisfied it was harsh, unjust or unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied the dismissal was harsh, unjust or unreasonable
      `my small business employer followed the Fair Dismissal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was a small business employer and complied with the Small Business Fair Dismissal Code
      `it was a genuine redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dismissal was a genuine redundancy (s 389)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I unfairly dismissed` IF
        `my employer ended my job, or forced me to resign`
    AND (NOT `only a fixed term, task or season ran out`)
    AND `if the FWC is satisfied it was harsh, unjust or unreasonable`
    AND (NOT `my small business employer followed the Fair Dismissal Code`)
    AND (NOT `it was a genuine redundancy`)

-- s 394(2): the application must be made "(a) within 21 days after the dismissal took effect; or (b) within such further
-- period as the FWC allows" for "exceptional circumstances".
@export Am I still in time to apply for an unfair dismissal remedy (s 394)?
GIVEN `days since the dismissal took effect` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since your dismissal took effect
      `if the FWC allows a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission allows more time for exceptional circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to apply for unfair dismissal` IF
        `days since the dismissal took effect` AT MOST 21
    OR  `if the FWC allows a further period`

-- s 392(5): compensation "must not exceed the lesser of: (a) the amount worked out under subsection (6) [the
-- remuneration for the 26 weeks immediately before the dismissal]; and (b) half the amount of the high income threshold
-- immediately before the dismissal."
@export What is the most compensation I can be awarded for an unfair dismissal (s 392(5))?
GIVEN `my remuneration for the last 26 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Remuneration received or owed for the 26 weeks before the dismissal, whichever is higher, in dollars
      `the high income threshold before the dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold immediately before the dismissal, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most compensation I can get` IS
    min `my remuneration for the last 26 weeks` (max `the high income threshold before the dismissal` `the high income threshold is never below` DIVIDED BY 2)

§§ `s 530 -- notice to Centrelink`

-- s 530(1): "If an employer decides to dismiss 15 or more employees for reasons of an economic, technological,
-- structural or similar nature ... the employer must give a written notice ... to ... Centrelink"; (3) "before
-- dismissing an employee".
@export Must my employer tell Centrelink before dismissing me with others (s 530)?
GIVEN `how many are to be dismissed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees your employer has decided to dismiss
      `for economic, technological, structural or similar reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reasons are economic, technological, structural or similar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer tell Centrelink` IF
        `how many are to be dismissed` AT LEAST 15
    AND `for economic, technological, structural or similar reasons`

§§ `s 536, regs 3.45-3.46 -- pay slips`

-- s 536(1): "within one working day of paying an amount to the employee in relation to the performance of work".
-- Reg 3.46(1): a pay slip "must specify: (a) the employer's name; (b) the employee's name; (c) the period ...; (d) the
-- date on which the payment ... was made; (e) the gross amount ...; (f) the net amount ...; (g) any amount ... that is a
-- bonus, loading, allowance, penalty rate, incentive-based payment or other separately identifiable entitlement; (h)
-- ... the Australian Business Number (if any) of the employer." (2) each deduction and where it went. (3) if paid
-- hourly: the ordinary rate, the hours, the amount at that rate. (4) if paid an annual rate: "the rate as at the latest
-- date". (5) if super contributions are made or intended: the amounts and the fund (with the (5A) exception for a new
-- employee whose fund is not yet known, not encoded).
@export Was my pay slip given in time (s 536(1))?
GIVEN `working days after I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days after the payment you got the pay slip
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my pay slip in time` IF
    `working days after I was paid` AT MOST 1

DECLARE PaySlip HAS
    `shows the employer's and my names` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows the pay period and payment date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows the gross and net amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows each bonus, loading, allowance or penalty rate paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows the employer's ABN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows each deduction and where it went` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows my hourly rate, hours and amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows my annual rate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shows the super contributions and fund` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does my pay slip contain everything the Regulations require (reg 3.46)?
GIVEN `my pay slip` IS A PaySlip @desc What your pay slip shows
      `my employer has an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has an Australian Business Number
      `amounts were deducted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anything was deducted from your gross pay
      `I am paid by the hour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid an hourly rate
      `I am paid an annual rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid an annual salary
      `my employer makes or will make super contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has made, or intends to make, superannuation contributions for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pay slip complete` IF
        `my pay slip`'s `shows the employer's and my names`
    AND `my pay slip`'s `shows the pay period and payment date`
    AND `my pay slip`'s `shows the gross and net amounts`
    AND `my pay slip`'s `shows each bonus, loading, allowance or penalty rate paid`
    AND ((NOT `my employer has an ABN`) OR `my pay slip`'s `shows the employer's ABN`)
    AND ((NOT `amounts were deducted`) OR `my pay slip`'s `shows each deduction and where it went`)
    AND ((NOT `I am paid by the hour`) OR `my pay slip`'s `shows my hourly rate, hours and amount`)
    AND ((NOT `I am paid an annual rate`) OR `my pay slip`'s `shows my annual rate`)
    AND ((NOT `my employer makes or will make super contributions`) OR `my pay slip`'s `shows the super contributions and fund`)

§§ `ss 544, 545, 548, reg 4.01 -- recovering an underpayment`

-- s 544: an application only "within 6 years after the day on which the contravention occurred". s 545(5): no order
-- "in relation to an underpayment that relates to a period that is more than 6 years before the proceedings concerned
-- commenced".
@export Am I in time to claim for this underpayment (ss 544, 545(5))?
GIVEN `years from the underpayment to my claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Years from the underpaid period to the day you start the claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to claim` IF
    `years from the underpayment to my claim` AT MOST 6

-- s 545(3): an eligible State or Territory court "may order an employer to pay an amount ... if the court is satisfied
-- that: (a) the employer was required to pay the amount under this Act or a fair work instrument; and (b) the employer
-- has contravened a civil remedy provision by failing to pay the amount."
@export Can the Magistrates Court order my employer to pay me what I am owed (s 545(3))?
GIVEN `my employer had to pay it under the Act or an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Act or a fair work instrument (such as an award) required your employer to pay the amount
      `my employer failed to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer failed to pay it, in breach of a civil remedy provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court order my employer to pay` IF
        `my employer had to pay it under the Act or an award`
    AND `my employer failed to pay it`

-- s 548(1): small claims proceedings if the claim is for an amount an employer was required to pay and the person
-- "indicates, in a manner prescribed by the regulations or by the rules of the court", that it wants the procedure.
-- Reg 4.01(1): by "endorsing the papers initiating the action" with that statement, or by lodging a paper that says so
-- (unless the court's rules prescribe the manner -- reg 4.01(2), an input). s 548(2): the court "may not award more
-- than: (a) $100,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations -- that higher amount". The deposited
-- Regulations prescribe no higher amount, so the cap is $100,000. (2A) interest does not count.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the small claims cap` MEANS 100000

@export Can my whole claim be dealt with as a small claim (s 548, reg 4.01)?
GIVEN `the amount I claim, without interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you claim, not counting interest, in dollars
      `I endorsed my papers or lodged a paper asking for the small claims procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your initiating papers say, or a paper you lodged says, that you want the small claims procedure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my claim be a small claim` IF
        `the amount I claim, without interest` AT MOST `the small claims cap`
    AND `I endorsed my papers or lodged a paper asking for the small claims procedure`
